+
+## Route-owned workspace and BF16 output
+
+Workspace planning covers every token width in the requested interval, including
+profile-specific Lt512 and tail fallbacks. Tile-only calls need no generic FP32
+plane or Q8 stream-k fixup. Mixed routes and distinct gathers retain their live
+buffers. NVFP4 keeps its existing conservative capacity contract.
+
+The BF16 Lt Store/Add route follows ninfer-5060-qwen@08c4fb70: FP32 accumulation,
+16-byte aligned BF16 output, column stride divisible by eight, and no GateProduct.
+FP32 destinations and unaligned BF16 calls retain the prior path. Weight decoding,
+actual per-group amax and E4M3/E8M0 coding are unchanged. Residual addition within
+GEMM may round differently; the numerical state/cost signature is profile-v3.
+The LinearAdd capacity query uses its known whole BF16 output; generic projection
+queries remain conservative for outputs whose type/layout is unknown.
+
+Validation is staged: public independent CPU/FP64 operations, exact capacities,
+BF16 Add Graph replay, sanitizer, same-GPU inference and fixed-corpus incremental
+PPL. These changes do not establish lossless FP8 or generalize 5060 Ti timings to
+other hardware. The 64 MiB weight image limit is still used at this stage.
